{:rows [{:response " Ifølge beskrivelsen av den _Endelige Tilstandsmaskinen_ i Altinn Formidling kan en filoverføring passere følgende tilstander fra den blir startet til filen eventuelt er slettet [1]:\n\n1. **Initialisert**\n2. **Opplasting pågår**\n3. **Sjekk av opplasting**\n4. **Publisert**\n5. **Nedlastinger initiert**\n6. **Alle bekreftet nedlastet**\n7. **Slettet**\n\nI tillegg finnes det to tilstander som representerer alternative utfall og som kan inntreffe istedenfor det ordinære løpet [1]:\n\n- **Avbrutt** – dersom overføringen avbrytes før noen nedlastingsprosess har startet.\n- **Overføring feilet** – dersom prosessen mislykkes under opplasting, behandling av opplasting eller under nedlasting hos en eller flere mottakere.\n\nDet er verdt å merke seg at ikke alle overføringer nødvendigvis ender i tilstanden **Slettet**. Kilden angir at filer kan forbli i _Altinn Broker File Store_ for å støtte fildeling for andre formål, og at den overordnede prosessen i slike tilfeller avsluttes etter at filen er lastet opp og **Publisert** [1].", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "ue-broker-01-filoverforing-tilstander", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :citation-recall 1.0, :completion-tokens 570, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 1.0, :config-id "deployed", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "altinn-broker,hard", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "dd56b73485fd6 R21.2 P3.6 h3.0 or0.7 L2169 3/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.1,0.0] +q | Basic concepts", :response-chars 1023, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 1, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 1, :golden-read? true, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "218bee00be34", :enrichment-hits 70, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 1.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 1, :prompt-tokens 6681, :pool-head "", :repeat 0, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "218bee00be34", :expected-chunk-ids "218bee00be34", :elapsed-ms 405791, :issued-queries "statuser filoverføring Altinn Formidling | file transfer status Altinn Formidling | filoverføring status livssyklus | Altinn Formidling file status states | status workflow filoverføring", :timestamp "2026-06-12T20:02:08.954087Z", :total-tokens 7251, :run-id "cfe0522e-6ac9-4a36-8170-dd9b84256596", :golden-display-rank 1, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 1.0} {:response " Modellfilene for en applikasjon ligger i mappen **`App/models/`** i app-repositoryet [1][2].\n\nIfølge kildene har en applikasjon fire modellfiltyper [1]:\n\n* **C# datamodell** (`<model>.cs`)\n* **JSON schema** (`<model>.schema.json`)\n* **XSD datamodell** (`<model>.XSD`)\n* **JSON-metadata** (`<model>.metadata.json`)\n\nHvilke filer som genereres, avhenger av arbeidsflyten:\n\n* Ved opplasting av en XSD-modell (`<model>.xsd`) genererer verktøyet filene **`<model>.cs`** og **`<model>.schema.json`** [2].\n* Ved å klikke på knappen **Generer modeller** i datamodelleringsverktøyet genereres det både **XSD- og C#-modellfiler** [3].\n\nI tillegg blir **JSON-metadata**-filen (`<model>.metadata.json`) generert ved behov, men den lagres **ikke** i applikasjonen [1].", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "ue-studio-03-datamodell-filer", :empty? false, :llm-calls 2, :citation-recall 1.0, :completion-tokens 642, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 1.0, :config-id "deployed", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "altinn-studio,hard", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "d87044ee89679 R22.5 P3.5 h3.0 or0.9 L1094 1/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.4,0.0,0.0] +q | Data modeling", :response-chars 756, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 4, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 1, :golden-read? true, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "3db5a48a99cd;e330142e8502;ae4d16c0c7ed;851c23f98303", :enrichment-hits 70, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 1.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 3, :prompt-tokens 5313, :pool-head "", :repeat 0, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "3db5a48a99cd;e330142e8502;ae4d16c0c7ed", :expected-chunk-ids "3db5a48a99cd", :elapsed-ms 569483, :issued-queries "modellfiler genereres app datamodell repo | app model files generated repository | datamodell genererte filer | model files generated app model repo | hvor ligger modellfiler i repo", :timestamp "2026-06-12T20:04:52.623053Z", :total-tokens 5955, :run-id "2a56c2e2-414c-4f3d-ab39-4b466e595a6c", :golden-display-rank 1, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 1.0} {:response " A XACML policy in Altinn describes access rules. According to [1] and [3], it can describe the following:\n\n- The Access rules for an APP created in Altinn Studio\n- The Access rules for a resource in Altinn Resource Registry\n- The Access rules for a correspondence or broker service in Altinn 3\n\nA policy consists of one or more rules [1][3][4].\n\nRegarding the parts that make up each rule, sources [1] and [3] explicitly state that each rule consists of three parts:\n\n- **Resources** — describes the resource a rule applies to [1][3]\n- **Action** — describes which action the rules apply to [1][3]\n- **Subject** — describes who the rules apply to [1][3]\n\nThere is some ambiguity across the sources: source [2] lists **Action**, **Subject**, **Obligation**, and **Condition** as descriptive elements, but it does not explicitly identify these as the constituent parts of a rule, and it notably omits **Resources**. Because [1] and [3] explicitly define a rule as consisting of three parts—Resources, Action, and Subject—those are the core components of a rule. Obligation and Condition appear as additional elements in the broader XACML policy context [2].", :terminal-clarification? false, :finish-reason "tool_calls", :golden-in-display? true, :question-id "ue-authz-05-xacml-policy-regelstruktur", :empty? false, :llm-calls 3, :citation-recall 1.0, :completion-tokens 460, :insufficiency-fired? false, :recall-at-10 1.0, :config-id "deployed", :clarification-rounds 0, :question-tags "altinn-authorization,hard", :cached-tokens 0, :golden-features "d9ed057e7daaa R25.3 P4.9 h4.0 or2.6 L3881 1/? ty:content+hypothetical-questions+metadata+phrase b[0.0,0.0,0.0,0.5,0.1,0.0] +q | Xacml", :response-chars 1156, :source "new", :search-passes 1, :n-retrieved 4, :reasoning-tokens 0, :golden-in-search-pool? true, :golden-pool-rank 1, :golden-read? true, :grounding-mode :chunks+answer, :answer-substring-hit? true, :retrieved-chunk-ids "c28fc018e0d0;7edbd10a3604;0b59b7d558d4;cfc9233eef06", :enrichment-hits 24, :n-expected 1, :status "complete", :recall-at-20 1.0, :refinement-corpus-grounded? nil, :n-cited 4, :prompt-tokens 5890, :pool-head "", :repeat 0, :error nil, :cited-chunk-ids "c28fc018e0d0;7edbd10a3604;0b59b7d558d4;cfc9233eef06", :expected-chunk-ids "c28fc018e0d0", :elapsed-ms 1133863, :issued-queries "XACML policy Altinn describe rule parts | XACML policy structure Altinn | XACML rule elements Altinn authorization", :timestamp "2026-06-12T20:14:17.004439Z", :total-tokens 6350, :run-id "c8e72531-70ea-46cd-8ec0-31f0f57e7cd2", :golden-display-rank 1, :steps-executed 3, :dataset "public-docs", :length-finish? false, :recall-at-5 1.0}], :out-dir "results/sweep-2026-06-12T19-55-22-404566Z", :csv-path "results/sweep-2026-06-12T19-55-22-404566Z/runs.csv"}
